     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Given:</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">df &lt;- data.frame(a = 1:6, b = rep(letters[1:3],2))</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">x &lt;- &#39;b&#39;</font></div><div><br></div><div>This works:</div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">group_by(df,b)</font></div><div><br></div><div>But why doesn&#39;t the following work?</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">group_by(df, x)</font></div><div><br></div><div>More crucially, neither does this:<br></div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">group_by(df, as.symbol(x)) </font>#failing with &quot;(list) object cannot be coerced to type &#39;symbol&#39;&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>And, of course, is there a fix?</div></div>"
